# Cloudflare Pages headers config: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# ── Security headers (all pages) ──────────────────────────────────
# CSP allows 'unsafe-inline' for script-src/style-src because the app is built
# entirely from inline <script> blocks and the Tailwind Play CDN (which injects
# a <style> tag at runtime) — a nonce/hash-based CSP would need a build step
# this project doesn't have. Still meaningfully reduces blast radius: blocks
# framing (clickjacking), restricts which hosts can load a script/style/font/
# XHR at all, and disables object/base-uri/form-action injection vectors.
#
# connect-src lists every external host the client actually calls: the
# open-meteo/nominatim/sunrise-sunset APIs used directly from the browser
# (label_data.html, degree_day_calculator.html), plus the Google Drive/OAuth
# hosts used by the Cloud Sync feature (public/sync/provider-gdrive.js) — that
# feature is currently disabled in the UI but not removed, so it's kept here
# to avoid a silent CSP break whenever it's turned back on.
#
# NOTE: Cache-Control is deliberately NOT set here. Two things were tried and
# both failed to actually take effect, verified against live response
# headers each time:
#   1. Separate `/*.js` / `/*.css` blocks — Cloudflare Pages' _headers path
#      matching doesn't support extension globs like that; it doesn't error,
#      it just silently never matches anything.
#   2. Cache-Control inside this same `/*` block — this pattern IS confirmed
#      to work (every other header here does reach .js/.css requests), but
#      Cloudflare Pages overrides Cache-Control specifically with its own
#      default asset policy (`max-age=14400`, ~4h) regardless.
# The actual fix lives in src/index.js's final catch-all: the Worker rewrites
# Cache-Control on the response itself after env.ASSETS.fetch() returns,
# which isn't subject to whatever Pages does internally with this file. See
# the comment there for why this matters (issue #33 — entotools.com and
# entotools.org, as separate custom domains on the same deployment, cache
# independently, so a stale edge cache on one could keep serving an old
# APP_VERSION for hours after a deploy).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.tailwindcss.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://accounts.google.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.open-meteo.com https://archive-api.open-meteo.com https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org https://api.sunrise-sunset.org https://www.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com https://oauth2.googleapis.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
